*> STRING statements whose operands delimited by size are longer than
*> the receiver. ON OVERFLOW, other delimiters, and operands of
*> unknown size are not counted against it.
IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. STRINGS.
DATA DIVISION.
WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
01  FIRST-NAME         PIC X(10) VALUE "ADA".
01  LAST-NAME          PIC X(15) VALUE "LOVELACE".
01  CODES.
    05  CODE-ENTRY     PIC X(4) OCCURS 3 VALUE "AB".
01  FULL-NAME          PIC X(20).
01  MESSAGE-TEXT       PIC X(30).
01  NARROW             PIC X(5).
PROCEDURE DIVISION.
    STRING FIRST-NAME DELIMITED BY SIZE
           " " DELIMITED BY SIZE
           LAST-NAME DELIMITED BY SIZE
        INTO FULL-NAME
    END-STRING
    STRING "CODE " CODE-ENTRY (2) " IS NOT VALID: "
           FIRST-NAME
        DELIMITED SIZE INTO MESSAGE-TEXT
    STRING FIRST-NAME DELIMITED BY SPACE
           " " DELIMITED BY SIZE
           LAST-NAME DELIMITED BY SPACE
        INTO FULL-NAME
    STRING FIRST-NAME LAST-NAME DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO FULL-NAME
        ON OVERFLOW DISPLAY "NAME TOO LONG"
    END-STRING
    STRING FUNCTION TRIM(LAST-NAME) DELIMITED BY SIZE
           ZERO DELIMITED BY SIZE
        INTO NARROW
    STRING LAST-NAME (1:4) "X" DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO NARROW
    STRING "ABCDE" DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO NARROW (2:3)
    DISPLAY FULL-NAME MESSAGE-TEXT NARROW
    GOBACK.
